{
  "info": {
    "name": "SCRUM-202 School reference data",
    "description": "Imports of the school reference data (docs/school-reference-data.md): school locations, FLDOE school grades and attendance zones. Every import is a background job (ingestion jobs, SCRUM-188) loaded with PostgreSQL COPY in one transaction per file (the SCRUM-201 loader). A file replaces only what it contains: its counties (schools, school-zones) or its school years (school-grades). Schools keep their id on reload.\n\nSetup: migrations V42 and V44 applied; the app started with INGESTION_STAGING_DIRECTORY set to the data root folder (the one that holds schools/), and INGESTION_INPUT_STORAGE=local for a single local instance. downloadedOn is the build date of the files (2026-11-22). Run folder 1 in order and send each job status request until COMPLETED. Set access_token when the ingestion routes require a token. No secret is stored in this file.\n\nReference data has no user ownership: it is public source data shared by every property, so the ownership checks of the ticket template do not apply; the scope checks are in the 'Invalid input' folder. The row counts, geometry validity, percentiles and lookup queries are checked in SQL (see the verification log of the docs).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{access_token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080"
    },
    {
      "key": "access_token",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "state",
      "value": "FL"
    },
    {
      "key": "downloadedOn",
      "value": "2026-11-22"
    },
    {
      "key": "schoolsFile",
      "value": "schools/schools.csv"
    },
    {
      "key": "gradesFile",
      "value": "schools/school_grades.csv"
    },
    {
      "key": "zonesFile",
      "value": "schools/school_zones.csv"
    },
    {
      "key": "jobId",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1 Imports (success)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1.1 Schools (31 counties)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('202 queued', () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));",
                  "const job = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('school reference job', () => { pm.expect(job.jobType).to.eql('REFERENCE_DATA_IMPORT'); pm.expect(job.dataset).to.eql('SCHOOLS'); pm.expect(job.status).to.be.oneOf(['QUEUED', 'RUNNING']); });",
                  "pm.test('Location points at the job', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Location')).to.eql('/api/ingestion/jobs/' + job.id));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('jobId', job.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/ingestion/import/schools?stagedFile={{schoolsFile}}&sourceState={{state}}&downloadedOn={{downloadedOn}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "ingestion",
                "import",
                "schools"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "stagedFile",
                  "value": "{{schoolsFile}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "sourceState",
                  "value": "{{state}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "downloadedOn",
                  "value": "{{downloadedOn}}"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "1.2 Job status (poll until COMPLETED)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const job = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('counters add up', () => pm.expect(job.processed).to.eql(job.completed + job.skipped + job.failed));",
                  "if (job.status === 'COMPLETED') {",
                  "  pm.test('every row loaded', () => { pm.expect(job.completed).to.eql(job.total); pm.expect(job.failed).to.eql(0); });",
                  "  pm.test('row count of the README (2114)', () => pm.expect(job.total).to.eql(2114));",
                  "} else { console.log('job is ' + job.status + ', send again'); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/ingestion/jobs/{{jobId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "ingestion",
                "jobs",
                "{{jobId}}"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
